# Meson build directories.
#
# The glob is the load-bearing line: meson drops a .gitignore inside every
# build directory it creates, so ad-hoc ones (build-check/, build-hw-check/,
# build-asan/, a bisect scratch dir) stayed untracked only by that accident.
# If a directory is ever created some other way — a partial `meson setup`, a
# manual mkdir, an unpacked artifact — the self-ignore is not there and the
# whole tree is suddenly staged. Name the pattern here instead of relying on
# the build system to hide its own output.
build*/

# Object files / artifacts
*.o
*.a
*.elf
*.bin

# Go build artifacts
cli/core
cli/core-*

# Test outputs
tests/runs/
tests/diffs/

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
